      "timestamp": "2026-05-28T18:52:33.396Z",
      "type": "message",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The product page is an `async` server component that awaits `getInventory()` before returning *any* JSX. Since `getInventory()` calls `connection()` (a dynamic API with a random/uncached result), the entire page — including the static `<h1>Premium Widget</h1>` title — is blocked until that dynamic data resolves. That's why the title doesn't appear immediately on navigation.\n\nThe fix is to stream: keep the static title outside the data fetch, and isolate the dynamic inventory in a child component wrapped in `<Suspense>`. The shell (including the title) renders instantly while the inventory streams in.",
      "raw": {
        "parentUuid": "651e3c31-07d2-422e-806b-05290d05e873",
        "isSidechain": false,
        "message": {
          "model": "claude-opus-4-8",
          "id": "msg_018266V4k2oaydGdefDSDqHh",
          "type": "message",
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The product page is an `async` server component that awaits `getInventory()` before returning *any* JSX. Since `getInventory()` calls `connection()` (a dynamic API with a random/uncached result), the entire page — including the static `<h1>Premium Widget</h1>` title — is blocked until that dynamic data resolves. That's why the title doesn't appear immediately on navigation.\n\nThe fix is to stream: keep the static title outside the data fetch, and isolate the dynamic inventory in a child component wrapped in `<Suspense>`. The shell (including the title) renders instantly while the inventory streams in."
            }
          ],
          "stop_reason": "tool_use",
