          "type": "message",
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Typecheck passes. Here's the change:\n\n**The problem:** `app/product/page.tsx` was an `async` component that `await`ed `getInventory()` before returning any markup. Because `getInventory()` calls `connection()` (an uncached dynamic API), Next.js had to block the *entire* page render — including the static `<h1>Premium Widget</h1>` title — until the inventory data resolved. So the whole page appeared at once, after the delay.\n\n**The fix:** I split the dynamic part into a child `Inventory` component wrapped in `<Suspense>`. Now:\n\n- `ProductPage` is a synchronous component, so its static shell — including the title — renders and streams to the browser **immediately** on navigation.\n- The inventory data (`count`/`price`) streams in afterward, showing `Loading inventory…` until it resolves.\n\nThe title now appears instantly while only the dynamic inventory waits for its data."
            }
          ],
